nc-guide-cyber-production-1 = [bold]Cyberware manufacturing[/bold]

nc-guide-cyber-production-2 = [bold]Production equipment[/bold]

nc-guide-cyber-production-3 = Every implant part is printed on the implant fabricator. Its board is printed on the circuit imprinter and assembly needs 4 micro manipulators. The ore processor supplies the metals. The cyberware bench is built from the construction menu: 12 steel sheets, 4 glass sheets, 6 cable and a screwdriver. Fit a charged standard battery.

nc-guide-cyber-production-4 = Every part has the same quality. The implant fabricator and the cyberware bench can be built where you need them.

nc-guide-cyber-production-5 = [bold]Muscle and bone reinforcement[/bold]

nc-guide-cyber-production-6 = 1. Print the muscle and bone reinforcement kit on the implant fabricator from steel, plastic and cloth.
    2. Place the kit on a cyberware bench with a charged battery. Use a sterile preparation wrap from the implant fabricator on the bench and wait for it to finish.

nc-guide-cyber-production-7 = [bold]Linear frames[/bold]

nc-guide-cyber-production-8 = Print the empty Sigma or Beta frame, anchors, controllers, sensor interfaces and power junctions on the implant fabricator.

nc-guide-cyber-production-9 = The normal actuator and the heavy Beta actuator are printed on the implant fabricator too.

nc-guide-cyber-production-10 = Mount the empty frame on the cyberware bench. Fit the actuator, controller, sensor interface, anchor kit and power junction. Beta uses its own heavy actuator and reinforced-anchor slots. Normal Sigma parts cannot fill these slots.

nc-guide-cyber-production-11 = Apply a standard firmware card to the occupied bench. Use the bench interaction menu to test the assembly. Tests require a charged cell, healthy components, sufficient rated power and thermal headroom. Sigma testing uses at least 50 energy, Beta 150. Changed parts or firmware invalidate the test.

nc-guide-cyber-production-12 = Use one sterile preparation pack on the occupied bench after a successful test. Preparation takes time and consumes another 50 energy for Sigma or 150 for Beta. The physical pack is consumed only after successful completion. Eject the prepared implant using the bench menu.

nc-guide-cyber-production-13 = [bold]Surgery[/bold]

nc-guide-cyber-production-14 = Manufacturing does not complete surgery. Sigma needs one fully integrated muscle/bone reinforcement set, Beta needs two. Install the frame through the chest; secure spinal and pelvic anchors and connect each limb through its own operative access. Beta also needs reinforced anchors. Then calibrate the implanted frame; Beta requires a separate powered load test.

nc-guide-cyber-production-15 = Extracted implants need new factory preparation before another installation. Damaged hardware retains its condition through disassembly and storage. A normal printed power cell fits the body bus; a separate special battery is not required.

nc-guide-cyber-production-16 = During movement in a slowing hardsuit, a powered frame draws additional energy and generates heat according to the suit penalty and its assistance limit. Stopping or removing the suit returns the motor to idle consumption. A jammed movement attempt still loads the motor.
